# Trusted tag signers — used by `.github/workflows/release.yml`
# `verify-tag-signature` job to gate release builds on the tag being
# signed by a key listed here (closes #716).
#
# This file is consulted via `git config gpg.ssh.allowedsignersfile`
# (see ADR 0005 §D-2). Format: one line per signer, `<principal>
# <key-type> <key-body>`. OpenSSH's `sshsig.c` skips `#`-prefixed
# lines anywhere in the file, so the explanatory header is safe to
# keep.
#
# Matching is by **key body**, not principal — git calls
# `ssh-keygen -Y find-principals` and accepts the signature if any
# principal in this file owns the key that produced it. The
# `<principal>` field is a label that documents which identity
# the key represents, not a constraint. An entry with a wildcard
# or wrong-but-plausible principal still grants release authority;
# treat every line as an unconditional grant.
